## Worksheet

**F1 — Core loop**: `GameState` class is the single state object; `SeededRandom` (Mulberry32-style) instantiated as `this.rng`, used for map, colonists, storms, events, caravan — no `Math.random` found; `endTurn()` calls processProduction→processNeeds→processMorale→processStorm→processRepairs→processCaravan→processEvents in fixed order. **Score: 2**

**F2 — Map**: 8x8 loop in `generateMap()`; terrain drawn via seeded `this.rng.next()`; `canBuild()` checks `terrain === required`; no adjacency-bonus code found anywhere. **Score: 1**

**F3 — Economy**: `mine` produces `ore`, `smelter` consumes `ore`→`metal` (real chain); `storageMax` enforced with overflow logged/clamped in `processProduction` and `buyGood`. **Score: 2**

**F4 — Population**: colonist records have skill/fatigue/morale/assigned; `processProduction` skillBonus reads only `c.level`, never `c.skill` string or `c.fatigue`. **Score: 1**

**F5 — Needs**: `processNeeds()` consumes food/water, shortage sets `col.morale -=20`; morale recovers `+10`/turn in `processMorale`; but morale never multiplies production output (only indirectly triggers colonist death). **Score: 1**

**F6 — Research**: 8 nodes in `initResearch`; `canResearch` checks `node.prereq` (used by `automation`); cost deducted in `doResearch`; `node.effects` object defined but never read anywhere else in the file. **Score: 1**

**F7 — Events**: 10 events array in `processEvents`; selection is uniform `rng.range`, not weighted; `eventCooldown` gates recently-fired events; **zero** events have choice branches — `showEventModal` always renders a single OK button. **Score: 1**

**F8 — Trade**: `goods` array in `renderTrade` has hardcoded buy/sell prices, not derived from `game.resources` or a drifting variable; `stock` param is not decremented on purchase (recreated each render); `buyGood`/`sellGood` both mutate `resources`/`scrip`. **Score: 1**

**F9 — Hazard**: `processStorm()` fires on `turn%12===0`, severity scales with `turn`; `building.damage` feeds `healthMul` in `processProduction`; `processRepairs` spends `parts` to reduce damage; `shield` building/`stormMitigation` research effect defined but never read in `processStorm`. **Score: 1**

**F10 — Save/load**: `save()` serializes full state to JSON string; `saveBtn` copies via clipboard/prompt; `GameState.load()` wraps `JSON.parse` in try/catch, `loadBtn` alerts `e.message` on failure. **Score: 2**

**F11 — End conditions**: `checkWin()` (turn≥60 & pop≥12) and `checkLose()` (pop===0) both called in `handleEndTurn`; `getScore()` combines population/research/resources/turns; `showEndScreen` renders modal breakdown. **Score: 2**

**F12 — UI**: tab-btn listeners toggle `.active`; log entries render `[Turn ${entry.turn}]`; tile/tree-node tooltips show produce/consume/damage/cost; keydown handler maps Space+1-6; `@media (max-width:600px)` adjusts layout. **Score: 2**

**F13 — Dev panel**: `runTests()` asserts storage caps, prereq enforcement, save/load round-trip, damage bounds — real invariants; `runBenchmark()` runs headless `GameState`, 200 `endTurn()` calls, prints `stateHash()`. **Score: 2**

**G1 — research→yield**: `research[key].effects` object written at `initResearch`/`doResearch` but no other function reads `.effects` anywhere; link absent. **Score: 0**

**G2 — shortfall→morale→output**: `processNeeds` shortage → `col.morale -= 20`; morale isn't a production multiplier, but morale<30 triggers `col.alive=false` in `processMorale`, removing them from `assigned` filter in `processProduction`, indirectly cutting output. **Score: 2**

**G3 — storm→damage→loss→repair→recovery**: `processStorm` sets `building.damage`; `processProduction` applies `healthMul = 1-damage*0.3`; `processRepairs` spends `parts`, decrements `damage`, restoring `healthMul` next turn. Fully traceable. **Score: 4**

**G4 — trade prices respond to stockpile/supply**: `goods` array in `renderTrade` has static numeric buy/sell fields; no read of `game.resources` or any drifting supply var. **Score: 0**

**G5 — event choices mutate state**: every event object has one `outcome()` and `showEventModal` builds a single OK button; no event offers branching choices at all. **Score: 0**

